    {
      "dom_id": "question-326521",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "There were approximately $28,\\,000$ factory jobs in the city in $2020.$  Economic forecasts predict that this number will grow by $35%$ by the year $2030.$  Which of the following is closest to the projected number of factory jobs in $2030?$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the projected number of jobs in $2030,$ we apply a $35%$ increase to the $2020$ figure.\n\nIncreasing by $35%$ means that we must apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+35%=135%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n135%=\\frac{135}{100}=1.35\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the new value by multiplying the original amount by $1.35:$\n\n$$\n28,\\,000\\times 1.35=37,\\,800\n$$\n\nTherefore, the projected number of factory jobs in $2030$ is $37,\\,800.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
      "problem_field_keys": [],
      "answer_fields_complete": null,
      "result": "Correct",
      "proof_feedback": null,
