      "raw_html": "<div class=\"question\" id=\"question-111226\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">3.</span><a class=\"questionKP\" href=\"/topics/79#10651\">Categorizing a Polynomial by Its Degree and Number of Terms</a><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"111226\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>Classify the polynomial <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"32\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2212\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mfrac><mjx-frac type=\"d\"><mjx-num><mjx-nstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-nstrut><mjx-mrow><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D461 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-mrow></mjx-num><mjx-dbox><mjx-dtable><mjx-line type=\"d\"></mjx-line><mjx-row><mjx-den><mjx-dstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-dstrut><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c35\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-den></mjx-row></mjx-dtable></mjx-dbox></mjx-frac></mjx-mfrac></mjx-mstyle></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mstyle></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> according to its degree and the number of terms.</p>\n</div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyModerate\">M</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Wed, Oct 14th @ 6:34 PM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 0:38</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: green;\">Correct</span></span></div></div>"
    },
    {
      "dom_id": "question-93111",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14220930/assets/2c4f090ff980be893416857fde0665bce955cee19f6a9dd7634039cbbcc641b6.png)\n\nAlex is making concrete using crushed stone and cement. The amount of cement he needs for a given amount of crushed stone is shown above. What is the ratio of crushed stone to cement in its simplest form?",
      "worked_solution": "One of the points belonging to the graph is $(60,15).$ Let's write the ratio $60:15$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{60}{15}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify this fraction by dividing both the numerator and the denominator by $15:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{60÷15}{15÷15}=\\frac{4}{1}\n$$\n\nSo the ratio of crushed stone to cement is $4:1.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
      "problem_field_keys": [],
      "answer_fields_complete": null,
      "result": "Correct",
      "proof_feedback": null,
