      "dom_id": "question-178541",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "The additive inverse of $30$ is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the additive inverse of the number $30$, we change its sign by placing a minus symbol $(-)$ in front of it. So, we obtain \n\n$$\n-\\,(30)=-30.\n$$\n\nTo check our work, we simply add the inverse to the original number. If we're correct, we should get zero.\n\n$$\n30+(-30)=30-30=0\\,✓\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
