      "name": null,
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14220930/assets/c4b96cbe8ea09940b84c1d9d03fc55bdb82c61388bfb66d99cc7c6abd847a1fd.png)\n\nThe inequality corresponding to the highlighted region shown above is $x${{field-1}}\n$-3\\text{ or }x$\n{{field-2}}$1.$",
      "worked_solution": "The red rays contain all values less than $-3,$ or greater than $1.$ In addition, \n\n- the closed circle at $-3$ implies that $x$ can be equal to $-3,$ and\n\n- the open circle at $1$ implies that $x$ cannot be equal to $1.$\n\nTherefore, the highlighted region represents $x\\le -3$ or $x>1.$",
