    {
      "dom_id": "question-53034",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14220930/assets/cd63e1c0cc60e53240ad8e064add8bd7c4d2abb1971de69a10b8f414b9c92fc8.png)\n\nWhich of the figures above is a square?",
      "worked_solution": "First, recall the hierarchy diagram of quadrilaterals, where each shape below another is a specific type of the one above it.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14220930/assets/1dbe4c3e8ea97c0ac077c37143802366c5817d86965ab1dbc5abf54cd01d27c3.png)\n\nRemember that a square is a quadrilateral where all angles are right and all sides are congruent.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each shape in turn.\n\n- The shape $P$ is a rhombus. Its four sides are congruent, however, it has no right angle. Therefore, it is not a square.\n\n- The shape $Q$ is a trapezoid. The sides are not all congruent, so it is not a square.\n\n- The shape $R$ is a kite. Since the sides are not all congruent, it is not a square.\n\n- The shape $S$ is an isosceles trapezoid. It has sides that are not congruent, therefore, it is not a square.\n\nTherefore, none of the shapes is a square.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
      "problem_field_keys": [],
      "answer_fields_complete": null,
      "result": "Incorrect",
      "proof_feedback": null,
      "html": "<div id=\"question-53034\" class=\"question\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">9.</span><a class=\"questionKP\" href=\"/topics/1459#2834\">Identifying a Quadrilateral</a><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"53034\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionGraphicFrame\"><img class=\"questionGraphic\" src=\"/graphics/q-53034\"></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>Which of the figures above is a square?</p>\n</div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyEasy\">E</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Wed, Oct 14th @ 6:34 PM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 0:00</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: red;\">Incorrect</span></span></div></div>",
