      "raw_html": "<div class=\"question\" id=\"question-162123\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">12.</span><a class=\"questionKP\" href=\"/topics/4136#12361\">Identifying Equivalent Fractions With Negative Numbers</a><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"162123\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>What is the missing part of the expression below?\n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"94\" display=\"true\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\" display=\"true\" style=\"margin-left: 0px; margin-right: 0px;\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2212\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mfrac><mjx-frac type=\"d\"><mjx-num><mjx-nstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-nstrut><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c39\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-num><mjx-dbox><mjx-dtable><mjx-line type=\"d\"></mjx-line><mjx-row><mjx-den><mjx-dstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-dstrut><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-den></mjx-row></mjx-dtable></mjx-dbox></mjx-frac></mjx-mfrac></mjx-mstyle><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mstyle space=\"4\"><mjx-mfrac><mjx-frac type=\"d\"><mjx-num><mjx-nstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-nstrut><mjx-mstyle style=\"border: 1pt solid black;\"><mjx-mpadded><mjx-block style=\"width: 0.95em; margin: 0.1em 0px; position: relative;\"><mjx-rbox style=\"left: 0.1em; top: 0px; max-width: 0.95em;\"><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mphantom><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D434 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-mphantom></mjx-texatom></mjx-rbox></mjx-block></mjx-mpadded></mjx-mstyle></mjx-num><mjx-dbox><mjx-dtable><mjx-line type=\"d\"></mjx-line><mjx-row><mjx-den><mjx-dstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-dstrut><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-den></mjx-row></mjx-dtable></mjx-dbox></mjx-frac></mjx-mfrac></mjx-mstyle></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"block\" unselectable=\"on\"><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mstyle style=\"border: 1pt solid black\"><mpadded depth=\"+1pt\" height=\"+1pt\" lspace=\"1pt\" width=\"+2pt\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mphantom><mi>A</mi></mphantom></mrow></mpadded></mstyle><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></p>\n</div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyEasy\">E</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Wed, Oct 14th @ 6:34 PM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 0:00</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: red;\">Incorrect</span></span></div></div>"
    },
    {
      "dom_id": "question-187260",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Complete the ratio table below.\n\n| $2$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $6$ |\n| {{field-2}} | $18$ |",
      "worked_solution": "We start with the ratio $4:6$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{6}\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the left-hand entry ($4$), and the denominator represents the right-hand entry ($6$).\n\nWe can generate equivalent ratios by finding equivalent fractions:\n\n- To create a numerator of $2,$ we divide the numerator and denominator of our fraction by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4÷2}{6÷2}=\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To create a denominator of $18,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator of the previous fraction by $6:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2\\times 6}{3\\times 6} & =\\frac{12}{18}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we fill in the ratio table:\n\n| $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $6$ |\n| $12$ | $18$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
