    {
      "dom_id": "question-113970",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14220930/assets/76d3a2d884ab6df8d6b6b97be5d5bac91ab30976ba0a6ef8aacc5f3a30eead6c.png)\n\nConsider the figure shown above. Which of the following triplets of points are collinear?\n\nI. $M,T,N$\n\nII. $S,T,O$\n\nIII. $P,Q,N$",
      "worked_solution": "- $M,T,N$ are collinear since there is a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14220930/assets/a3574ff790eadbc561d842f7c2b485d055a76f5781da76afbd7fb39e45e7ccf0.png)\n\n- $S,T,O$ are collinear since there is a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14220930/assets/4ca9c5bbfc7c0f95a5bc03e6e84102eb362cba63d937a184089584a7c2ad58bf.png)\n\n- $P,Q,N$ are **not** collinear since we can't draw a straight line that passes through all of them.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14220930/assets/6b5e9a5c1e1fa271c93667c35c117b197cec3d5a25e5ac311e77f0021663163d.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
      "problem_field_keys": [],
      "answer_fields_complete": null,
      "result": "Incorrect",
      "proof_feedback": null,
      "html": "<div id=\"question-113970\" class=\"question\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">14.</span><a class=\"questionKP\" href=\"/topics/1500#10748\">Determining Whether Points on Intersecting Lines Are Collinear</a><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"113970\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionGraphicFrame\"><img class=\"questionGraphic\" src=\"/graphics/q-113970\"></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>Consider the figure shown above. Which of the following triplets of points are collinear?</p>\n<ol class=\"questionStatements\"><li>  <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"122\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D440 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D447 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D441 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> </li><li>  <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"123\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D446 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D447 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D442 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistiv