    {
      "dom_id": "question-93124",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "A tank with a capacity of $2\\,000$ liters is filled with $1\\,400$ liters of water. What percentage of the tank is filled with water?",
      "worked_solution": "We're given a part and a whole, and we must find a percentage. So, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{percentage}=\\text{part}÷\\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn this case, \n\n- the part is the amount of water, which is $1\\,400$ liters, and\n\n- the whole is the capacity of the tank, which is $2\\,000$ liters.\n\nSubstituting our numbers into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\text{percentage}=1\\,400÷2\\,000=\\frac{14}{20}.\n$$\n\nTo write this as a percentage, we create an equivalent fraction with $100$ as the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{14}{20}=\\frac{14\\times 5}{20\\times 5}=\\frac{70}{100}\n$$\n\nNow we can write this fraction as a percentage:\n\n$$\n\\frac{70}{100}=70%\n$$\n\nTherefore, $70%$ of the tank is filled with water.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
      "problem_field_keys": [],
      "answer_fields_complete": null,
      "result": "Incorrect",
      "proof_feedback": null,
      "html": "<div id=\"question-93124\" class=\"question\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">15.</span><a class=\"questionKP\" href=\"/topics/3754#2333\">Finding a Missing Percent Given Two Numbers Without Simplification</a><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"93124\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>A tank with a capacity of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"128\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mspace style=\"width: 0.167em;\"></mjx-mspace></mjx-mstyle><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace></mstyle><mn>000</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> liters is filled with <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"129\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mspace style=\"width: 0.167em;\"></mjx-mspace></mjx-mstyle><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c34\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace></mstyle><mn>400</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> liters of water. What percentage of the tank is filled with water?</p>\n</div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficul